---
import DemoTelemetry from './DemoTelemetry.astro';
import ExecutionOrigin from './ExecutionOrigin.astro';
import { ADAPTER_SOURCE_URL, crateLayerHref, crateLayerPin, liveCrateLayers } from '../data/live-runtime';
import { STATIC_DEMO_STATUS } from '../runtime/demo-runtime';
import { auditedBrowserTopology } from '../runtime/neuromorphic-adapter';
import { staticMeshGeometry } from '../runtime/topology-layout';
import '../styles/hero.css';

// The homepage hero hosts the live demo island. Its first paint is a static
// drawing of the exact network the live path runs: the audited topology the
// browser bridge requires of every Rust/WASM snapshot, laid out and coloured
// by the renderer's own rules. WebGL later draws over the same reserved box,
// so nothing moves when it takes over. The surrounding hero copy comes from
// the page through the slots.
const topology = auditedBrowserTopology();
const mesh = staticMeshGeometry(topology);
const nodeCount = mesh.nodes.length;
const edgeCount = mesh.edges.length;
const nodePath = mesh.nodes.map((node) => `M${node.x} ${node.y}h0`).join('');
---
<div class="live-hero" data-neuromorphic-demo>
  <section class="hero hero-live" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <slot name="heading" />
    <div class="hero-text"><slot /></div>
    <figure class="hero-mesh" data-demo-viewport>
      <div class="hero-mesh-stage">
        <div class="demo-surface" data-demo-surface role="img" aria-label="Live drawing of the same network, from Rust/WASM snapshots" hidden></div>
        <svg class="hero-mesh-static" viewBox={mesh.viewBox} role="img" aria-labelledby="hero-mesh-title hero-mesh-desc">
          <title id="hero-mesh-title">Static drawing of the live network</title>
          <desc id="hero-mesh-desc">{`${nodeCount} neurons on a ring, joined by the ${edgeCount} synapses that synaptic-wiring defines. Excitatory synapses are rust and inhibitory ones dark grey; weaker synapses fade toward grey. This is the network the Rust/WASM simulation runs, drawn at build time.`}</desc>
          <g class="hero-mesh-edges" stroke-opacity={mesh.edgeOpacity}>
            {mesh.edges.map((edge) => <line x1={edge.x1} y1={edge.y1} x2={edge.x2} y2={edge.y2} stroke={edge.stroke} />)}
          </g>
          <path class="hero-mesh-nodes" d={nodePath} stroke={mesh.nodeFill} stroke-width={mesh.nodeSizePx} />
        </svg>
        <p class="hero-mesh-input"><span data-input="scripted">input: scripted path</span><span data-input="pointer">input: your pointer</span></p>
        <button type="button" class="button button-secondary hero-mesh-play" data-demo-play hidden>Play animation</button>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="hero-mesh-caption">
        <div class="hero-mesh-meta">
          <ExecutionOrigin origin="static-diagram" runtimeBound />
          <span class="hero-mesh-mode">
            <span data-when="idle">{nodeCount} neurons · {edgeCount} synapses</span>
            <span data-when="live">{nodeCount} neurons · {edgeCount} synapses · simulating in this browser</span>
          </span>
        </div>
        <ol class="crate-trail" aria-label="Crate layers behind the live simulation, in pipeline order">
          {liveCrateLayers.map((layer) => (
            <li><a href={crateLayerHref(layer)}>{layer.name}</a> <span class="crate-pin">{crateLayerPin(layer)}</span></li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <p class="hero-mesh-links"><a href="#live-telemetry">Inspect the live runtime <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a href="/labs/">Explore the labs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
        <p class="demo-status" data-demo-status role="status" aria-live="polite">{STATIC_DEMO_STATUS}</p>
        <noscript>
          <p class="demo-status demo-status-noscript">JavaScript is required for the live visualization. Navigation and the rest of this page remain available.</p>
        </noscript>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <slot name="index" />
  </section>
  <section class="hero-runtime" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
    <div class="hero-runtime-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Neuromorphic demo</p>
      <h2 id="demo-title">Every pulse traces back to a crate.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-runtime-copy">
      <p class="demo-copy">Every 50 ms the site turns your pointer, or a scripted path when nobody is interacting, into one <code>[x, y, pressure]</code> packet. <code>kinetic-signals</code> turns it into 16 features, <code>axon-encoder</code> encodes them as spikes, <code>neuromod</code> steps its LIF neurons, and <code>synaptic-wiring</code> owns the synapses and delays each pulse travels along. The <a href={ADAPTER_SOURCE_URL}>adapter crate</a> composes them into one WebAssembly module; the canvas only draws what it returns.</p>
      <p class="demo-copy">Before WebAssembly and WebGL start, and whenever they cannot, the drawing above is the same network: it is rendered at build time from the topology the browser bridge requires of every live snapshot. Native CUDA and FPGA results are <a href="/evidence/">recorded separately</a> and never run in this browser, and recorded <a href="/protocol/">protocol data</a> has its own page.</p>
    </div>
    <DemoTelemetry />
  </section>
</div>
<script>
  import { enhanceNeuromorphicDemos } from '../runtime/enhance-demo';
  try {
    enhanceNeuromorphicDemos();
  } catch {
    // Keep static navigation and explanatory content available.
  }
</script>
